-- the composition, in percent, as a function of the form: 36 for the alpha anomer and 64 for the beta, at
-- 25 C in water. It is a function of the condition and not of either structure, which is what makes a
-- mixture's identity an observation and not a formula -- Mix and mix-frac-differs above say the same for
-- UVCB substances, and a sugar in water is the same statement in a case nobody would call a UVCB.
glu-fraction : Nat → Nat
glu-fraction x = case eqb x 0 of true → 36; false → 64
